    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d691">

                <pb facs="0978" n="862" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg862"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.51637/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crowder</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-04-17T23:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">April 17,
                                1923—11 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 18—2:10
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>17. Reference to your number 33, April 17, 4 p.m. Department will of course have
                    in mind its number 159 of September 29, 1921, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="33"
                        xml:id="d691-f1"/> transmitting designation by New York Federal Reserve Bank
                    of the National City Bank as its Cuban agent under section 14, Federal Reserve
                    Act. I understand however that this agency has not actively engaged in the
                    transaction of business prescribed in that section. Believe conditions favorable
                    to the success of an agency which will engage actively in the transaction of
                    such business and that opportune announcement that one will be established will
                    be helpful in the present crisis.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crowder</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
